<article class="env-lemma" id="07SR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07SR">Lemma <span data-tag="07SR">70.5.11</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Situation <a href="/tag/084R" data-tag="084R">70.5.5</a>. If $X$ is a scheme, then there exists an $i$ such that $X_ i$ is a scheme. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a finite affine open covering $X = \bigcup W_ j$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0827" data-tag="0827">70.5.7</a> we can find an $i \in I$ and open subspaces $W_{j, i} \subset X_ i$ whose base change to $X$ is $W_ j \to X$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/07SQ" data-tag="07SQ">70.5.10</a> we may assume that each $W_{j, i}$ is an affine scheme. This means that $X_ i$ is a scheme (see for example Properties of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/03JG" data-tag="03JG">66.13</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>